## Family Intake Fields

| Field | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Family label | Yes | Example: Carol family or Wick family. |
| Primary contact name | Yes | Person approving setup and payment. |
| Primary contact phone | Yes | SMS delivery number. |
| Care recipient name | Yes | Use approved display name. |
| Delivery window | Yes | Daily time range for SMS note. |
| Care note purpose | Yes | What the family wants the note to accomplish. |
| Source input method | Yes | Manual, form, caregiver SMS, agency update, or other. |
| Tone preference | Recommended | Warm, concise, faith-friendly, neutral, detailed, etc. |
| Topics to avoid | Recommended | Medical details, financial details, family conflict, etc. |
| Beta price | Yes | $15-20/month. |
| Payment status | Yes | Pending, confirmed, paused, canceled. |
| First test sent | Yes | Date and result. |

## Daily Channel Posting Rhythm

- Post one onboarding update whenever a beta family moves to a new setup step.
- Post one confirmation when a daily care note is generated.
- Post immediately when SMS delivery fails or needs a retry.
- Post concise family feedback after each first-week check-in.
- Post beta payment confirmation only after payment is actually received.

## First #rennxai-carenotes Channel Update

*care-notes beta kickoff update*

We are moving care-notes.com into beta setup. This stays separate from CRM activity and revenue tracking; this channel is only for care-notes family onboarding, daily note confirmations, SMS issues, family feedback, and beta payment updates.

Current beta target:
- Get 3-5 families live and paying
- Start with Carol and Wick, then add the next families
- Validate daily care note usefulness before bundling this into the larger CRM offer
- Confirm beta pricing at $15-20/month per family

First onboarding pass:
- Confirm primary family contact and SMS number
- Confirm care recipient display name
- Confirm daily note purpose and preferred delivery window
- Run first test note
- Send first SMS test
- Capture family feedback
- Confirm payment before counting the family as live

Today I am treating the beta as live setup, not theory. The first goal is simple: get the first family through test note, SMS confirmation, feedback, and payment status.

